  "note": "Lean replaces the Euler–Maclaurin step by the counting bound |N_S(y) − S/(4y)| ≤ 1; the main term ¼Σg₂(m)log(1+1/m) is the same. Erratum: (5.30) prints f'(3/2m), f'(s/(m+1)), (2m/s)^2, ((m+1)/s)^2 where S is meant, and its variation step is wrong: f' has total variation 6(m+1)^2/S^2 and |f'(S/2m-)| = 2m^2/S^2, so the stated Euler-Maclaurin method gives (m+1)^2/(2S^2) (odd n: (m+1)^2/S^2), which is at most the printed c_{v,0}(5m^2+2m+1)/S^2 only for m >= 3. (checked by `scripts/checks/eq_5_30.py`)."
